Original integration code is licensed under Apache-2.0.

The downloaded Unitree Go2 model and meshes come from
unitreerobotics/unitree_mujoco, commit
1eb6642e3f3fdfb7fb13a9794fd6a2dd93ea0e7d, BSD-3-Clause.
The original license is preserved as .runtime/assets/model/LICENSE.

The Go2 robot_lab policy, configuration, and observation/action conventions
are from Ziqi Fan's fan-ziqi/rl_sar, commit
376d42c9b128f963ab08579762d5a216a976ce39, Apache-2.0.
The original license is preserved as .runtime/assets/policy/LICENSE.
go2_sim/controller.py implements those observation/action conventions for
named MuJoCo joints and adds a separately documented yaw feedback adapter.
No policy weights or vendor model source bytes are changed.

Optional handstand inference conventions and unmodified ONNX models are from
Sang-SC/go2_quad2hand, bd410e4d91d3fabc1bedf1348fabe64542446e96,
BSD-3-Clause; see third_party/quad2hand-LICENSE.txt.
Optional backflip inference conventions and unmodified ONNX model are from
Robot-Nav/GO2_backflip, 732ddac12eafc7191e66ca3364c5ace35a675349,
MIT; see third_party/backflip-LICENSE.
stunt-assets.lock.json pins downloads and SHA256 checksums. Adapters translate
named joints and observations; they do not change the robot model parameters.

Robonix and its Python API are separately installed dependencies, not vendored
here. Consult their upstream licenses. This package is a community integration,
not a claim of Unitree endorsement or proprietary Sport-controller equivalence.
